{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792680183454,"sessionID":"ses_e9bef9eb5ffei9kgkpy3SKTJAg","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call-90af7845-35c2-424c-a256-935197662f2e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-22\\20-brief.md"},"output":"<path>C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-22\\20-brief.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Brief — 2026-10-22\n2: \n3: ## The use case\n4: \n5: FRC media students write a recap post after every event their team plays (2-8\n6: per season plus the October-December offseason circuit running right now), and\n7: the numbers they quote - qual rank, W-L-T record, alliance selection, playoff\n8: finish, awards, district points - all live on the team's The Blue Alliance\n9: event page (\"Team 9128 was Rank 1 with a record of 17-0-0 ... Captain of\n10: Alliance 1 and won the event\"). The community's reaction to the season-level\n11: FRC Rewind web app (\"Now I have something other than Spotify Wrapped!\")\n12: shows the appetite for a rendered card; this template is the per-event,\n13: batchable, self-hosted version of that idea.\n14: \n15: ## The template\n16: \n17: - id: `@one-a-day/sports/frc-event-recap/v1` — pack `sports`, no new pack:\n18:   FRC is a team competition with quals, playoffs and records, and the pack\n19:   already holds the chess, cubing, sim-racing and powerlifting recap cards.\n20: - title: `FRC Event Recap` (the scaffold prefixes `2026-10-22 · `, tags\n21:   `day-033`).\n22: - kind: image (still PNG); canvas hint `1080x1080` (the Instagram feed the\n23:   recap graphics are made for); must also render cleanly at landscape\n24:   (`1920x1080`, the Chief Delphi / X post) and portrait (`1080x1920`, the\n25:   story) - and pass the build's 7-canvas layout sweep (1920x1080 · 1280x720\n26:   · 1080x1920 · 1080x1080 · 3840x2160 · 640x360 · 480x270).\n27: - duration: still (no clock; `outputHints.format { kind: \"image\",\n28:   container: \"png\" }`).\n29: \n30: ## Layout (regions, ratios — no pixels)\n31: \n32: Square/portrait stack five bands; landscape splits header+hero left and\n33: chips+awards right, footer full-width below.\n34: \n35: ```\n36: +------------------------------------------+\n37: | FRC EVENT RECAP        [accent rule]     | header ~24%: the label,\n38: | TEAM 9128                                | the team number as the hero\n39: | Harbor City District - Week 4            | line, event + week line,\n40: | (IRON PANTHERS when teamName set)        | optional team name in caps\n41: +------------------------------------------+\n42: |  RANK 1          |   17-0-0              | hero ~26%: qual rank with\n43: |  of 48 teams     |   W - L - T           | \"of N teams\", the record\n44: +------------------------------------------+\n45: | [CAPTAIN - ALLIANCE 1]  [EVENT WINNER]   | chips ~14%: alliance\n46: |                                          | selection + playoff finish\n47: +------------------------------------------+\n48: | AWARDS                                   | awards ~24%: 0-3 lines,\n49: |  + Innovation in Control Award           | accent tick each; an empty\n50: |  + (a second award)                      | list returns the space\n51: +------------------------------------------+\n52: | 78 DISTRICT POINTS   DATA: THE BLUE ALL. | footer ~8%: points left\n53: |                                          | (0 hides), TBA credit right\n54: +------------------------------------------+\n55: ```\n56: \n57: The one design decision: **the card derives what it can and constrains the\n58: rest to The Blue Alliance's own vocabulary.** Rank, team count, record and\n59: district points are numbers; the alliance and playoff chips come from enums\n60: (\"captain\" / \"1st pick\" / \"2nd pick\", alliance 1-8; winner / finalist /\n61: semifinalist / quarterfinalist) so their text always fits. Awards are the\n62: one free text on the card - the scout's flagged risk, since TBA award names\n63: run long - so they are capped at three lines and shrink to fit above the\n64: readability floor, never ellipsized at it.\n65: \n66: ## Layout contract (the invariants the build sweeps at 7 canvases)\n67: \n68: - Every text fits its box — `textFitsMeasured` on each text source (header\n69:   lines, both hero numbers, both chip texts, each award line, both footer\n70:   texts).\n71: - The team number is the top-of-card identity: `team-number` within\n72:   `yFrac [0, 0.3]`.\n73: - The footer band is at the bottom: `footer-points` and `footer-credit`\n74:   within `yFrac [0.85, 1]`; the credit is always present.\n75: - The hero pair is present: `rank-number` and `record-text` (bare labels).\n76: - Chips are present when their props say so (at defaults, both):\n77:   `alliance-chip` and `playoff-chip` bare labels.\n78: - The awards block is present when the list is non-empty: `awards-label`\n79:   within the middle band `yFrac [0.45, 0.9]`; an empty list reserves no\n80:   band.\n81: - No exact fractions pinned beyond those bands - the reflow between square\n82:   bands and landscape columns is the template's own business.\n83: \n84: ## Props (13 + debugLayout)\n85: \n86: | name | type | default | what it changes | required |\n87: |---|---|---|---|---|\n88: | `teamNumber` | number | `9128` | the hero line \"TEAM 9128\" (1-99999, FRC numbers are digits) | no |\n89: | `teamName` | string | `\"\"` | the team nickname in caps under the number (<= 30 ASCII); \"\" removes the line (the default renders the scout's cited TBA page, number only) | no |\n90: | `eventName` | string | `\"Harbor City District\"` | the event line (<= 40 ASCII; invented default) | no |\n91: | `weekLabel` | string | `\"Week 4\"` | printed after the event name, \" - \" joined (<= 20 ASCII: \"Week 4\", \"DCMP\", \"Offseason\"); \"\" removes it | no |\n92: | `qualRank` | number | `1` | the RANK hero (1-200) | no |\n93: | `teamCount` | number | `48` | the \"of 48 teams\" line under the rank (0-200; 0 hides it); when > 0, `qualRank` above it is refused | no |\n94: | `record` | string | `\"17-0-0\"` | the record hero, validated as W-L-T digits | no |\n95: | `allianceRole` | enum | `\"captain\"` | alliance chip: `captain` / `pick1` / `pick2` -> \"CAPTAIN - ALLIANCE N\" / \"1ST PICK - ALLIANCE N\" / \"2ND PICK - ALLIANCE N\"; `none` hides the chip | no |\n96: | `allianceNumber` | number | `1` | the N on the alliance chip (1-8; ignored when role is `none`) | no |\n97: | `playoffResult` | enum | `\"winner\"` | playoff chip: \"EVENT WINNER\" / \"FINALIST\" / \"SEMIFINALIST\" / \"QUARTERFINALIST\"; `none` hides it | no |\n98: | `awards` | json | `[\"Innovation in Control Award\"]` | 0-3 award lines, each <= 60 ASCII (real TBA names run long), shrunk to fit above the floor | no |\n99: | `districtPoints` | number | `78` | the footer-left \"78 DISTRICT POINTS\" (0-999; 0 hides, e.g. regionals and offseason) | no |\n100: | `accent` | string color | `\"#2f7bff\"` | the one accent: header rule, chip outlines, award ticks (a TBA-ish blue) | no |\n101: | `debugLayout` | boolean | `false` | draws the layout contract over the card | no |\n102: \n103: Derived helpers (pure, exported, unit-tested): `allianceChipText(role,\n104: allianceNumber)`, `playoffChipText(result)`, `recordText(wlt)` after format\n105: validation, `rankSub(teamCount)` (\"\" when 0). All copy composed from these -\n106: no chip or line is hand-typed free text except awards, eventName, weekLabel\n107: and teamName, which are length-capped and shrink-fitted.\n108: \n109: ## Beats\n110: \n111: Still — no beats.\n112: \n113: ## Defaults must show\n114: \n115: A viewer with no inputs sees the scout's cited TBA example as a finished\n116: card: **TEAM 9128** at the Harbor City District - Week 4, **RANK 1** of 48\n117: teams with a **17-0-0** record, the chips **CAPTAIN - ALLIANCE 1** and\n118: **EVENT WINNER**, one award line (Innovation in Control Award), **78\n119: DISTRICT POINTS** and the \"DATA: THE BLUE ALLIANCE\" credit, one blue accent\n120: on a dark page - a card a media student could post as-is.\n121: \n122: ## Acceptance rubric (the critic scores against this)\n123: \n124: 1. At defaults the card renders complete - header (label, team number,\n125:    event + week), rank + record heroes, both chips, one award line, footer\n126:    points + credit - with no clipped or overlapping text at any of the\n127:    seven contract canvases.\n128: 2. The derived copy is right: `record \"17-0-0\"` prints as-is and bad\n129:    formats are refused by name; `allianceRole \"pick1\"` + `allianceNumber 4`\n130:    prints \"1ST PICK - ALLIANCE 4\"; `playoffResult \"finalist\"` prints\n131:    \"FINALIST\"; `teamCount 0` drops the \"of N teams\" line; `districtPoints\n132:    0` drops the footer-left text but keeps the TBA credit.\n133: 3. Impossible input is refused by name: `qualRank` above a non-zero\n134:    `teamCount`, a `record` that is not W-L-T digits, an `allianceNumber`\n135:    outside 1-8 with a playing role, a fourth award, a non-ASCII or overlong\n136:    award/event/team string.\n137: 4. The three aspects reflow without loss: square and portrait stack the\n138:    five bands, landscape puts header+hero left and chips+awards right with\n139:    the footer full-width, and the layout contract holds on all seven\n140:    canvases (award lines - the long free text - are the stress case).\n141: 5. Deterministic and honest: identical props give an identical document, no\n142:    clock, no `Math.random`, a misspelled prop is refused by name, all\n143:    default copy is printable ASCII, and the card reads at a glance as an\n144:    FRC event recap (team number as identity, chips scannable, numbers no\n145:    logos).\n146: \n147: ## Variants worth trying (each ONE idea different)\n148: \n149: - **a — dark social card:** the baseline above, square-first, dark page,\n150:   one blue accent; the Instagram posture.\n151: - **b — wide-first:** hint `1920x1080` and lead with the two-column\n152:   arrangement (header+hero left, chips+awards right) — the Chief Delphi / X\n153:   header-image posture; same props, different composition.\n154: - **c — light paper preset:** the square banded layout on a light page with\n155:   dark ink — the newsletter / team-website print posture.\n\n(End of file - total 155 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Brief — 2026-10-22\n\n## The use case\n\nFRC media students write a recap post after every event their team plays (2-8\nper season plus the October-December offseason circuit running right now), and\nthe numbers they quote - qual rank, W-L-T record, alliance selection, playoff\nfinish, awards, district points - all live on the team's The Blue Alliance\nevent page (\"Team 9128 was Rank 1 with a record of 17-0-0 ... Captain of\nAlliance 1 and won the event\"). The community's reaction to the season-level\nFRC Rewind web app (\"Now I have something other than Spotify Wrapped!\")\nshows the appetite for a rendered card; this template is the per-event,\nbatchable, self-hosted version of that idea.\n\n## The template\n\n- id: `@one-a-day/sports/frc-event-recap/v1` — pack `sports`, no new pack:\n  FRC is a team competition with quals, playoffs and records, and the pack\n  already holds the chess, cubing, sim-racing and powerlifting recap cards.\n- title: `FRC Event Recap` (the scaffold prefixes `2026-10-22 · `, tags","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"C:\\src\\m0saic-production\\one-a-day\\journal\\2026-10-22\\20-brief.md","text":"# Brief — 2026-10-22\n\n## The use case\n\nFRC media students write a recap post after every event their team plays (2-8\nper season plus the October-December offseason circuit running right now), and\nthe numbers they quote - qual rank, W-L-T record, alliance selection, playoff\nfinish, awards, district points - all live on the team's The Blue Alliance\nevent page (\"Team 9128 was Rank 1 with a record of 17-0-0 ... Captain of\nAlliance 1 and won the event\"). The community's reaction to the season-level\nFRC Rewind web app (\"Now I have something other than Spotify Wrapped!\")\nshows the appetite for a rendered card; this template is the per-event,\nbatchable, self-hosted version of that idea.\n\n## The template\n\n- id: `@one-a-day/sports/frc-event-recap/v1` — pack `sports`, no new pack:\n  FRC is a team competition with quals, playoffs and records, and the pack\n  already holds the chess, cubing, sim-racing and powerlifting recap cards.\n- title: `FRC Event Recap` (the scaffold prefixes `2026-10-22 · `, tags\n  `day-033`).\n- kind: image (still PNG); canvas hint `1080x1080` (the Instagram feed the\n  recap graphics are made for); must also render cleanly at landscape\n  (`1920x1080`, the Chief Delphi / X post) and portrait (`1080x1920`, the\n  story) - and pass the build's 7-canvas layout sweep (1920x1080 · 1280x720\n  · 1080x1920 · 1080x1080 · 3840x2160 · 640x360 · 480x270).\n- duration: still (no clock; `outputHints.format { kind: \"image\",\n  container: \"png\" }`).\n\n## Layout (regions, ratios — no pixels)\n\nSquare/portrait stack five bands; landscape splits header+hero left and\nchips+awards right, footer full-width below.\n\n```\n+------------------------------------------+\n| FRC EVENT RECAP        [accent rule]     | header ~24%: the label,\n| TEAM 9128                                | the team number as the hero\n| Harbor City District - Week 4            | line, event + week line,\n| (IRON PANTHERS when teamName set)        | optional team name in caps\n+------------------------------------------+\n|  RANK 1          |   17-0-0              | hero ~26%: qual rank with\n|  of 48 teams     |   W - L - T           | \"of N teams\", the record\n+------------------------------------------+\n| [CAPTAIN - ALLIANCE 1]  [EVENT WINNER]   | chips ~14%: alliance\n|                                          | selection + playoff finish\n+------------------------------------------+\n| AWARDS                                   | awards ~24%: 0-3 lines,\n|  + Innovation in Control Award           | accent tick each; an empty\n|  + (a second award)                      | list returns the space\n+------------------------------------------+\n| 78 DISTRICT POINTS   DATA: THE BLUE ALL. | footer ~8%: points left\n|                                          | (0 hides), TBA credit right\n+------------------------------------------+\n```\n\nThe one design decision: **the card derives what it can and constrains the\nrest to The Blue Alliance's own vocabulary.** Rank, team count, record and\ndistrict points are numbers; the alliance and playoff chips come from enums\n(\"captain\" / \"1st pick\" / \"2nd pick\", alliance 1-8; winner / finalist /\nsemifinalist / quarterfinalist) so their text always fits. Awards are the\none free text on the card - the scout's flagged risk, since TBA award names\nrun long - so they are capped at three lines and shrink to fit above the\nreadability floor, never ellipsized at it.\n\n## Layout contract (the invariants the build sweeps at 7 canvases)\n\n- Every text fits its box — `textFitsMeasured` on each text source (header\n  lines, both hero numbers, both chip texts, each award line, both footer\n  texts).\n- The team number is the top-of-card identity: `team-number` within\n  `yFrac [0, 0.3]`.\n- The footer band is at the bottom: `footer-points` and `footer-credit`\n  within `yFrac [0.85, 1]`; the credit is always present.\n- The hero pair is present: `rank-number` and `record-text` (bare labels).\n- Chips are present when their props say so (at defaults, both):\n  `alliance-chip` and `playoff-chip` bare labels.\n- The awards block is present when the list is non-empty: `awards-label`\n  within the middle band `yFrac [0.45, 0.9]`; an empty list reserves no\n  band.\n- No exact fractions pinned beyond those bands - the reflow between square\n  bands and landscape columns is the template's own business.\n\n## Props (13 + debugLayout)\n\n| name | type | default | what it changes | required |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `teamNumber` | number | `9128` | the hero line \"TEAM 9128\" (1-99999, FRC numbers are digits) | no |\n| `teamName` | string | `\"\"` | the team nickname in caps under the number (<= 30 ASCII); \"\" removes the line (the default renders the scout's cited TBA page, number only) | no |\n| `eventName` | string | `\"Harbor City District\"` | the event line (<= 40 ASCII; invented default) | no |\n| `weekLabel` | string | `\"Week 4\"` | printed after the event name, \" - \" joined (<= 20 ASCII: \"Week 4\", \"DCMP\", \"Offseason\"); \"\" removes it | no |\n| `qualRank` | number | `1` | the RANK hero (1-200) | no |\n| `teamCount` | number | `48` | the \"of 48 teams\" line under the rank (0-200; 0 hides it); when > 0, `qualRank` above it is refused | no |\n| `record` | string | `\"17-0-0\"` | the record hero, validated as W-L-T digits | no |\n| `allianceRole` | enum | `\"captain\"` | alliance chip: `captain` / `pick1` / `pick2` -> \"CAPTAIN - ALLIANCE N\" / \"1ST PICK - ALLIANCE N\" / \"2ND PICK - ALLIANCE N\"; `none` hides the chip | no |\n| `allianceNumber` | number | `1` | the N on the alliance chip (1-8; ignored when role is `none`) | no |\n| `playoffResult` | enum | `\"winner\"` | playoff chip: \"EVENT WINNER\" / \"FINALIST\" / \"SEMIFINALIST\" / \"QUARTERFINALIST\"; `none` hides it | no |\n| `awards` | json | `[\"Innovation in Control Award\"]` | 0-3 award lines, each <= 60 ASCII (real TBA names run long), shrunk to fit above the floor | no |\n| `districtPoints` | number | `78` | the footer-left \"78 DISTRICT POINTS\" (0-999; 0 hides, e.g. regionals and offseason) | no |\n| `accent` | string color | `\"#2f7bff\"` | the one accent: header rule, chip outlines, award ticks (a TBA-ish blue) | no |\n| `debugLayout` | boolean | `false` | draws the layout contract over the card | no |\n\nDerived helpers (pure, exported, unit-tested): `allianceChipText(role,\nallianceNumber)`, `playoffChipText(result)`, `recordText(wlt)` after format\nvalidation, `rankSub(teamCount)` (\"\" when 0). All copy composed from these -\nno chip or line is hand-typed free text except awards, eventName, weekLabel\nand teamName, which are length-capped and shrink-fitted.\n\n## Beats\n\nStill — no beats.\n\n## Defaults must show\n\nA viewer with no inputs sees the scout's cited TBA example as a finished\ncard: **TEAM 9128** at the Harbor City District - Week 4, **RANK 1** of 48\nteams with a **17-0-0** record, the chips **CAPTAIN - ALLIANCE 1** and\n**EVENT WINNER**, one award line (Innovation in Control Award), **78\nDISTRICT POINTS** and the \"DATA: THE BLUE ALLIANCE\" credit, one blue accent\non a dark page - a card a media student could post as-is.\n\n## Acceptance rubric (the critic scores against this)\n\n1. At defaults the card renders complete - header (label, team number,\n   event + week), rank + record heroes, both chips, one award line, footer\n   points + credit - with no clipped or overlapping text at any of the\n   seven contract canvases.\n2. The derived copy is right: `record \"17-0-0\"` prints as-is and bad\n   formats are refused by name; `allianceRole \"pick1\"` + `allianceNumber 4`\n   prints \"1ST PICK - ALLIANCE 4\"; `playoffResult \"finalist\"` prints\n   \"FINALIST\"; `teamCount 0` drops the \"of N teams\" line; `districtPoints\n   0` drops the footer-left text but keeps the TBA credit.\n3. Impossible input is refused by name: `qualRank` above a non-zero\n   `teamCount`, a `record` that is not W-L-T digits, an `allianceNumber`\n   outside 1-8 with a playing role, a fourth award, a non-ASCII or overlong\n   award/event/team string.\n4. The three aspects reflow without loss: square and portrait stack the\n   five bands, landscape puts header+hero left and chips+awards right with\n   the footer full-width, and the layout contract holds on all seven\n   canvases (award lines - the long free text - are the stress case).\n5. Deterministic and honest: identical props give an identical document, no\n   clock, no `Math.random`, a misspelled prop is refused by name, all\n   default copy is printable ASCII, and the card reads at a glance as an\n   FRC event recap (team number as identity, chips scannable, numbers no\n   logos).\n\n## Variants worth trying (each ONE idea different)\n\n- **a — dark social card:** the baseline above, square-first, dark page,\n  one blue accent; the Instagram posture.\n- **b — wide-first:** hint `1920x1080` and lead with the two-column\n  arrangement (header+hero left, chips+awards right) — the Chief Delphi / X\n  header-image posture; same props, different composition.\n- **c — light paper preset:** the square banded layout on a light page with\n  dark ink — the newsletter / team-website print posture.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":155,"totalLines":155,"truncated":false}},"title":"journal\\2026-10-22\\20-brief.md","time":{"start":1792680183090,"end":1792680183436}},"id":"prt_16410c51e001zNbtzth3xyY0ou","sessionID":"ses_e9bef9eb5ffei9kgkpy3SKTJAg","messageID":"msg_16410b4870016mv7VhCuOhrhMe"}}
